{
 "esm": "2.0.0",
 "metadata": {
 "name": "cam_rrtmg_solver",
 "description": "The CAM RRTMG shortwave column solver (stage 2 of the EqESM project) as math, transcribed from the instrumented cam6_4_212 fork (components/cam/src/physics/rrtmg/aer_src/rrtmg_sw_cldprmc.f90, ext/rrtmg_sw/rrtmg_sw_reftra.f90, rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90, rrtmg_sw_vrtqdr.f90; the longwave rtrnmc/rtrnmc sweeps are not yet transcribed): the McICA delta-M cloud scaling (cldprmc_sw inflag = 0, rrtmg_sw_cldprmc.f90:94-113, reusing the delta-scaling laws of the CICE dEdd scheme, same algebra), the PIFM two-stream layer reflectance/transmittance (reftra_sw kmodts = 2, rrtmg_sw_reftra.f90:129-291) with the Meador-Weaver gamma coefficients as model-scoped law templates, the direct-beam layer transmittance (spcvmc_sw, rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90:555-593, the Pade-table law in closed form) as a law template, and the adding method (vrtqdr_sw, rrtmg_sw_vrtqdr.f90:96-230) as one-sided lag-1 faq interface recurrences with the zreflect factor inlined (the CLI rejects the coupled recurrence written with a shared zreflect intermediate as an observed cycle, esm-spec 4.9.6; see README.md for the probe). The models are composed by data: each model declares its inputs (parameters with dump-derived defaults); stage-3 composition will couple them by reference. All layer and interface axes are the RRTMG top-down k = 1..33 (k = 1 the clear extra top layer, rrtmg_sw_rad.f90:859-874), k_ifc = 1..34, and the bottom-up kb = 1..34 (kb = 1 at the surface, reading the top-down layer NK+2-j); the esd lev_nodes axis (1 = surface) carries the output fluxes with the k_ifc = 1 cell dropped. The gpt axis is the pinned 4-member subset {1, 9, 13, 47} of the 112 RRTMG g-points (members 1..4 in that order). The pins are the gated cam_rad_spcvmc.csv/cam_rad_spcvmc_ifc.csv dump of the solver internals (the cam_dump_spcvmc_sw buffer of cam_dump_mod.F90, called at the end of the spcvmc_sw g-point loop of the climate icall = 0 pass, flushed at the radiation boundary): the expected values are dump columns only - the delta-M scaled cloud optics taucmc_ds/ssacmc_ds/asmcmc_ds, the clear (ztauc/zomcc/zgcc) and total (ztauo/zomco/zgco) member layer optics, the layer reftra outputs (zrefc/zrefdc/ztrac/ztradc clear member, zrefo/zrefdo/ztrao/ztrado total member), the layer direct-beam transmittances (zdbtc clear, zdbt total) and their interface cumulants (ztdbtc/ztdbt), the vrtqdr interface flux fractions (zcd/zcu clear, zfd/zfu total), and the per-g-point fluxes zincflx*zcd..zfu (pfd_c/pfu_c/pfd/pfu) - with the McICA subcolumn cloud fields of cam_rad_solver_sw.csv (cld_sto/tauc_sto/ssac_sto/asmc_sto/fsfc_sto) and the cam_rad_scal.csv solar geometry as inputs. The two sky members are distinct at the cloudy cells (the total member carries the delta-scaled cloud, rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90:501-508). The k-distribution optics before the spcvmc dump site are not dumped; the CloudScale model is pinned on the dumped masked cloud fields and the dumped post-scaling optics, and the Layer/DirectBeam/Adding/Fluxes models on the dumped layer optics, layer law outputs, flux fractions and per-g-point fluxes. Every expected value is selected (not derived) by extract_cam_rrtmg_solver_pins.py, and every test description cites the RRTMG g-point and the dump column.",
 "tags": [
  "atmosphere",
  "cam",
  "rrtmg",
  "shortwave",
  "two-stream",
  "dump-pinned",
  "cesm"
 ],
 "created": "2026-11-24T00:00:00Z",
 "authors": [
  "EqESM project contributors"
 ],
 "references": [
  {
   "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM: CAM6 physics sources of the instrumented cam6_4_212 fork (components/cam/src/) - aer_src/rrtmg_sw_cldprmc.f90, aer_src/rrtmg_sw_reftra.f90, aer_src/rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90, aer_src/rrtmg_sw_vrtqdr.f90, aer_src/rrtmg_sw_rad.f90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
   "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
  },
  {
   "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
   "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
  }
 ]
},
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 32,
   "description": "Number of CAM model layers (pver = 32); the esd column axis lev (1 = surface) and its NLEV+1 interfaces lev_nodes."
  },
  "NK": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 33,
   "description": "Number of RRTMG layers of the solver columns (klev = 33, num_rrtmg_levs): the 32 CAM layers plus the clear extra top layer, k = 1..33 top-down."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 4,
   "description": "Number of pinned RRTMG shortwave g-points carried by the gpt axis (members 1..4 = RRTMG g-points 1, 9, 13, 47 of the ngptsw = 112; the k-distribution gas optics are not dumped, so the solver is pinned on this subset)."
  },
  "NBND": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 14,
   "description": "Number of RRTMG shortwave bands (nbndsw = 14)."
  },
  "NSKY": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 2,
   "description": "Sky members of the shortwave layer solution: 1 = clear-sky member (the reftra_sw call on the clear optics, lrtchkclr all true), 2 = total-sky member (the reftra_sw call on the total optics, lrtchkcld, blended into the clear member by the McICA cloud fraction, rrtmg_sw_spcvmc.f90:536-553, and consumed by the second vrtqdr_sw call of :598-602)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "k": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NK"
  },
  "k_ifc": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "NK",
     1
    ]
   }
  },
  "kb": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "NK",
     1
    ]
   }
  },
  "gpt": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NGPT"
  },
  "band": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NBND"
  },
  "sky": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "NSKY"
  },
  "lev_nodes": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     "NLEV",
     1
    ]
   }
  }
 },
 "models": {
